enchilada: GPU: v1 DCVS perf and bandwidth tables, then raise the GPU level (gpulvl=)

The GPU ran at its boot level: gpu_gx_rail_on() votes the 257 MHz ARC indices (VLVL 64) and HFI
start sent only INIT, FW_VER and TEST, so the GMU never had a perf table and nothing asked for
more (four full-screen 1125x2436 draws took ~67 ms of GPU time, gl-run-23). Now the v1 start
does what Linux a6xx_hfi_start_v1 does between FW_VERSION and TEST (after TEST the GMU takes no
more HFI messages): H2F_MSG_PERF_TABLE (id 4, a6xx_hfi_msg_perf_table_v1, 43 dwords: 8 GPU
levels = Linux's gmu->gpu_freqs for sdm845, 0/257/342/414/520/596/675/710 MHz in kHz, each with
the ARC vote a6xx_gmu_rpmh_arc_votes_init builds from cmd-db gfx.lvl (primary, first index at or
above the OPP's opp-level) and mx.lvl (secondary, first at or above it, else the highest
non-zero); 3 GMU levels 0/200/400 MHz from cx.lvl/mx.lvl at MIN_SVS/SVS) and H2F_MSG_BW_TABLE
(id 3, 160 dwords, a6xx_build_bw_table verbatim: one "off" DDR level and the fixed CNOC votes,
the a630 GMU does no bus scaling). Once GX is up and the core answers, before the CP's hw_init
(where Linux's a6xx_gmu_set_initial_freq runs), the legacy a6xx_gmu_set_freq sequence asks for
the level: GMU_DCVS_ACK_OPTION (0x23fc) = 0, GMU_DCVS_PERF_SETTING (0x23fd) = 3 << 28 | index,
GMU_DCVS_BW_SETTING (0x23fe) = 0xff, OOB DCVS_SET (set bit 23, ack bit 31, clear bit 31), then
GMU_DCVS_RETURN (0x23ff) must read 0. On this phone's cmd-db (gfx 0 16 48 64 128 192 256 320
384 416, mx 0 16 16 256 384) the votes are 0x400303 (257 MHz, the indices the boot already uses)
... 0x1800408 (675) and 0x1a00409 (710, mx at its top 384 as Linux does). Boot-arg gpulvl=N: the
default is the highest level whose VLVL gfx.lvl and mx.lvl both hold exactly (6, 675 MHz here);
gpulvl=7 is Linux's 710 MHz; 0 sends the tables but keeps the boot level; 1 sends neither (the
behaviour before this patch); anything else is 1. Any missing table, unacknowledged message or
level outside gfx.lvl leaves the boot level alone. One line per boot:
"SWEET GPU: DCVS level N (X MHz, bw idx 255): acked|failed".

